# Secrets and key material
# ·················
# A node holds the operator's keys and its deployment configuration: whatever
# holds them must never be committed. These patterns are deliberately broad — a
# false positive costs one `git add -f`, a false negative is unrecoverable once
# pushed.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.crt
*.cer
*.der
*.jks
*.keystore
*.age
*.sops.*
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
*.secrets.*
*.local.*

# Never commit non-public notes
# ·················
*.private.*
*.internal.*
*.notes.md
NOTES*.md

# Build output
# ·················
/target/
**/*.rs.bk
*.autogen.*

# Profiling output
# ·················
*.profraw
*.profdata
flamegraph.svg
perf.data
perf.data.old

# Node runtime state
# ·················
# SQLite stores (NODE_JOURNAL, NODE_OUTBOX), their WAL sidecars and the lock
# file of the process that runs the background tasks.
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-shm
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite.background.lock
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite3-shm
*.sqlite3-wal
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal

# Files the node and its examples write in the working directory: the
# system-foundation/1 statement (CERTCRYPT_SYSTEM_FOUNDATION_PATH, or the
# output of the gen_dev_foundation example), the operator domain binding
# state (NODE_DOMAIN_BINDING_STATE) and the well-known file
# (NODE_WELL_KNOWN_FILE). They describe a deployment, not this repository.
/system-foundation.json
*.system-foundation.json
/node-domain-binding.json
/node-domain-binding.json.lock
/certcrypt-node.json

# Logs
# ·················
*.log

# Editors and OS
# ·················
.vscode/
.idea/
.history/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# Scratch
# ·················
/tmp/
/TMP/
.tmp/
*.tmp
*.bak
